uestion-bc7ca1bb-54ce-5dca-bfc4-11a992a5eb47" :question/answer-fields "answer-field-7e001f08-93a9-56c4-8f18-23859cf513f4"] [17592186110674 :knowledge-point/questions "question-bc7ca1bb-54ce-5dca-bfc4-11a992a5eb47"] ["question-65844bd9-30e0-51e9-84e5-199c9f665392" :question/id #uuid "65844bd9-30e0-51e9-84e5-199c9f665392"] ["question-65844bd9-30e0-51e9-84e5-199c9f665392" :question/math-academy-id "q-93124"] ["question-65844bd9-30e0-51e9-84e5-199c9f665392" :question/problem "A tank with a capacity of $2\\,000$ liters is filled with $1\\,400$ liters of water. What percentage of the tank is filled with water?"] ["question-65844bd9-30e0-51e9-84e5-199c9f665392" :question/worked-solution "We're given a part and a whole, and we must find a percentage. So, we can use the following formula:\n\n$$\n\\text{percentage}=\\text{part}÷\\text{whole}\n$$\n\nIn this case, \n\n- the part is the amount of water, which is $1\\,400$ liters, and\n\n- the whole is the capacity of the tank, which is $2\\,000$ liters.\n\nSubstituting our numbers into the above formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\text{percentage}=1\\,400÷2\\,000=\\frac{14}{20}.\n$$\n\nTo write this as a percentage, we create an equivalent fraction with $100$ as the denominator:\n\n$$\n\\frac{14}{20}=\\frac{14\\times 5}{20\\times 5}=\\frac{70}{100}\n$$\n\nNow we can write this fraction as a percentage:\n\n$$\n\\frac{70}{100}=70%\n$$\n\nTherefore, $70%$ of the tank is filled with water."] ["question-65844bd9-30e0-51e9-84e5-199c9f665392" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate] ["answer-field-50ca2ce7-e417-59bb-aca3-04e72dab4b49" :answer-field/id #uuid "50ca2ce7-e417-59bb-aca3-04e72dab4b49"] ["answer-d0e81f18-8cc4-5e74-904b-b57c090b0e0b" :answer/id #uuid "d0e81f18-8cc4-5e74-904b-b57c090b0e0b"] ["answer-d0e81f18-8cc4-5e74-904b-b57c090b0e0b" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-d0e81f18-8cc4-5e74-904b-b57c090b0e0b" :answer/value "60%"] ["answer-be3b0c24-e0bc-506c-9198-80272d7ce629" :answer/id #uuid "be3b0c24-e0bc-506c-9198-80272